{"name":"Succulent Greenhouse","hex":"#8ba477","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"succulent","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Juicy or lush.","Luscious or delectable."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A succulent plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/succulent"},{"term":"greenhouse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A building used to grow plants, particularly one with large glass windows or plastic sheeting to trap heat from sunlight even in intemperate seasons or climates. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The glass of a plane's cockpit."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place (plants) in a greenhouse.","To nurture in order to promote growth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greenhouse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Succulent plant","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, succulent plants, also known as succulents, are plants with parts that are thickened, fleshy, and engorged, usually to retain water in arid climates or soil conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Split_Aloe.jpg/330px-Split_Aloe.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Succulent_plant"},{"title":"Greenhouse","blocks":[{"text":"In horticulture, a greenhouse is a structure designed to regulate the temperature and humidity of the environment inside it with a view to growing plants.\nThere are different types of greenhouses, but they all have large areas covered with transparent materials that let sunlight enter and that inhibit the loss of the sun's heat. The most common materials used in modern greenhouses for walls and roofs are rigid plastics made of polycarbonate, plastic film made of polyethylene, or glass panes. When sunlight shines into a greenhouse the temperature inside increases, providing a sheltered environment for plants to grow — even in cold weather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Botanical_Garden_V.L._Komarov_Botanical_Institute.jpg/330px-Botanical_Garden_V.L._Komarov_Botanical_Institute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenhouse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Succulent_in_San_Francisco.JPG/500px-Succulent_in_San_Francisco.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Succulent_in_San_Francisco.JPG/1280px-Succulent_in_San_Francisco.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Succulent_in_San_Francisco.JPG/500px-Succulent_in_San_Francisco.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The center rosette of Aloe polyphylla","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASucculent_in_San_Francisco.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Eze_jardin_exotique.JPG/500px-Eze_jardin_exotique.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Eze_jardin_exotique.JPG/1280px-Eze_jardin_exotique.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Eze_jardin_exotique.JPG/500px-Eze_jardin_exotique.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A collection of succulent plants, including cacti, from the Jardin botanique d'Èze, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEze_jardin_exotique.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Succulents_in_habitat_Adromischus_marianiae%2C_Crassula_deceptor_and_Conophytum.jpg/500px-Succulents_in_habitat_Adromischus_marianiae%2C_Crassula_deceptor_and_Conophytum.jpg?utm_s